      <h2>What's Next?</h2>
      <p>
        This project was only the beginning of my journey with Power BI. Since then, I've continued exploring data analysis using SQL, Python, Tableau, and Power BI, with a particular interest in financial and business data.
      </p>
      <p>
        My next goal is to build increasingly complex projects that combine data cleaning, statistical analysis, visualisation, and predictive modelling. I'm also interested in exploring how these tools can be used to support better financial and strategic decision-making.
      </p>

      <h2>Final Thoughts</h2>
      <p>
        Building my first Power BI dashboard taught me that data analytics is not simply about knowing how to use a particular software tool. It is about asking the right questions, understanding the data, finding meaningful patterns, and communicating those findings clearly.
      </p>
      <p>
        For anyone who is just starting with Power BI, my biggest advice is simple: <strong>Don't wait until you know everything before building your first project.</strong>
      </p>
      <p>
        Start with a dataset, ask a few questions, build something, make mistakes, and improve it. That's how I learned—and I'm still learning.
      </p>
      <p>
        This is just one project in my journey from mathematics to data science and financial analytics. Thanks for reading, and I'll see you in the next article.
      </p>
